# Table loading

Search and filter, when rows are already on screen, do not replace the table with a skeleton. The rows stay. The table body dims, and one loader is visible on the table itself.

The search field, the table header, and the page caption are not dimmed. An empty response and an error stay as text. A timed journal refresh does not turn the loader on. The first visit, when there are no rows yet, is still a skeleton.

There is one loader, in `HoldRegion`. Do not add a second library or a second spinner. The mark is one `Skeleton` bar in the center of the table, over the dimmed rows. The region is marked `aria-busy`.

```tsx
<HoldRegion held={held}>{rows}</HoldRegion>
```
